00:00:58.013 --> 00:01:00.690
(gentle music)

00:01:00.690 --> 00:01:02.490
And so we start with the Americanist

00:01:02.490 --> 00:01:05.910
of American freedoms, the
right to own flamethrowers,

00:01:05.910 --> 00:01:08.710
and of course, other
extremely deadly weapons.

00:01:08.710 --> 00:01:10.930
When politicians and judges decide

00:01:10.930 --> 00:01:12.160
the meaning of the Second Amendment,

00:01:12.160 --> 00:01:13.740
it's often the context of determining

00:01:13.740 --> 00:01:15.140
what types of weapons should

00:01:15.140 --> 00:01:17.880
or should not be in the hands
of a civilian population.

00:01:17.880 --> 00:01:19.830
That was the line pre-president Joe Biden

00:01:19.830 --> 00:01:22.260
took in a 2019 interview
with Anderson Cooper

00:01:22.260 --> 00:01:24.710
while arguing in favor of
an assault weapons ban.

00:01:24.710 --> 00:01:26.480
- Look, the second amendment doesn't say

00:01:26.480 --> 00:01:30.080
you can't restrict the kinds
of weapons people can own.

00:01:30.080 --> 00:01:31.840
You can't buy a bazooka.

00:01:31.840 --> 00:01:33.380
You can't have a flamethrower.

00:01:33.380 --> 00:01:34.560
- Well actually, Mr. President,

00:01:34.560 --> 00:01:37.110
it turns out that you
can own a flamethrower.

00:01:37.110 --> 00:01:40.170
You also can own a bazooka
with some restrictions.

00:01:40.170 --> 00:01:42.190
In fact, there are a
variety of high powered

00:01:42.190 --> 00:01:45.850
and deadly weapon you can
legally own in the United States.

00:01:45.850 --> 00:01:48.140
Under the National Firearms Act of 1934,

00:01:48.140 --> 00:01:50.660
as revised by the Gun Control Act of 1968

00:01:50.660 --> 00:01:55.020
and the Omnibus Crime Control
and Safe Streets Act of 1968,

00:01:55.020 --> 00:01:57.730
individuals can legally
acquire sawed off shotguns,

00:01:57.730 --> 00:01:59.710
any automatic weapons like machine guns

00:01:59.710 --> 00:02:02.440
made before 1986, and destructive devices

00:02:02.440 --> 00:02:05.940
like grenades, mortars,
and yes, even bazookas.

00:02:05.940 --> 00:02:07.850
But I'm sorry to tell
you that these weapons,

00:02:07.850 --> 00:02:11.160
commonly known as Title II
weapons or NFA firearms,

00:02:11.160 --> 00:02:13.740
can only be acquired after
passing a background check,

00:02:13.740 --> 00:02:16.100
paying a $200 transfer tax,

00:02:16.100 --> 00:02:17.500
registering the weapon with the ATF,

00:02:17.500 --> 00:02:19.840
and obtaining the approval
of the Attorney General.

00:02:19.840 --> 00:02:21.230
Though, a few states like Delaware,

00:02:21.230 --> 00:02:23.150
New York, and California
prohibit ownership

00:02:23.150 --> 00:02:26.080
of all certain types of Title II weapons,

00:02:26.080 --> 00:02:28.770
but most states allow
for the legal ownership

00:02:28.770 --> 00:02:31.470
if the owner has complied
with federal registration

00:02:31.470 --> 00:02:33.060
and taxation requirements.

00:02:33.060 --> 00:02:35.160
Oh, and FYI, if you decide to shoot

00:02:35.160 --> 00:02:36.520
a missile in South Carolina,

00:02:36.520 --> 00:02:39.550
you can do it as long as
you get a permit first.

00:02:39.550 --> 00:02:40.660
Fun fact.

00:02:40.660 --> 00:02:43.260
Flame throws are an entirely
different animal though.

00:02:43.260 --> 00:02:45.210
Believe it or not, there is no federal law

00:02:45.210 --> 00:02:47.420
governing the private
use of flamethrowers,

00:02:47.420 --> 00:02:50.440
also known as extended reach torches.

00:02:50.440 --> 00:02:51.980
In fact, only two states in the country

00:02:51.980 --> 00:02:54.000
have any restrictions
on flamethrowers at all,

00:02:54.000 --> 00:02:55.460
Maryland and California.

00:02:55.460 --> 00:02:56.950
Maryland flat out bans the device,

00:02:56.950 --> 00:02:59.170
while California only
allows you to obtain one

00:02:59.170 --> 00:03:01.430
if you get a permit from
the state fire marshal.

00:03:01.430 --> 00:03:02.263
And as you may know,

00:03:02.263 --> 00:03:04.660
Elon Musk has even gotten
into the flamethrower game

00:03:04.660 --> 00:03:06.860
by selling his own propane powered,

00:03:06.860 --> 00:03:09.020
not a flamethrower device,

00:03:09.020 --> 00:03:11.260
named to head off issues
with customs officials.

00:03:11.260 --> 00:03:12.980
However, people who have tried to take

00:03:12.980 --> 00:03:14.880
his product overseas have often found

00:03:14.880 --> 00:03:16.160
that customs officials disagree

00:03:16.160 --> 00:03:18.620
that this device is not a flamethrower,

00:03:18.620 --> 00:03:20.920
landing these people in
legal trouble abroad.

00:03:20.920 --> 00:03:23.220
And like many other topics
discussed in this video,

00:03:23.220 --> 00:03:26.970
you may be asking how on
earth is this possibly legal?

00:03:26.970 --> 00:03:29.290
After all flamethrowers were
historically a weapon of war,

00:03:29.290 --> 00:03:31.150
especially during World War II.

00:03:31.150 --> 00:03:32.590
- [Narrator] A flame throwing tank stops

00:03:32.590 --> 00:03:34.320
the mass funeral fire.

00:03:34.320 --> 00:03:36.410
There is no eulogy and no mourning.

00:03:36.410 --> 00:03:38.070
- But contrary to their portrayals

00:03:38.070 --> 00:03:39.130
in movies and video games,

00:03:39.130 --> 00:03:42.260
flamethrowers are classified
as tools, not weapons.

00:03:42.260 --> 00:03:43.880
And as tools, flamethrowers

00:03:43.880 --> 00:03:45.910
actually have a wide
variety of legitimate uses

00:03:45.910 --> 00:03:49.040
outside of your garden variety
cartoon super villainy.

00:03:49.040 --> 00:03:50.590
Flamethrowers can be
used to clear vegetation,

00:03:50.590 --> 00:03:52.800
quickly melt snow from your driveway,

00:03:52.800 --> 00:03:54.020
can be used to quickly sanitize

00:03:54.020 --> 00:03:56.670
stadium seats in what's
known as flame polishing.

00:03:56.670 --> 00:03:58.290
They're great for cooking steaks,

00:03:58.290 --> 00:04:00.820
and don't tell anyone,
but they work really well

00:04:00.820 --> 00:04:04.820
in training dogs and cats,
though it only works once.

00:04:04.820 --> 00:04:07.910
Now, despite all of these
completely legitimate uses,

00:04:07.910 --> 00:04:09.580
state and federal lawmakers from New York

00:04:09.580 --> 00:04:11.040
have tried to ban the device.

00:04:11.040 --> 00:04:13.740
In response to Musk's
not a flamethrower stunt,

00:04:13.740 --> 00:04:15.530
New York State lawmakers introduced a bill

00:04:15.530 --> 00:04:17.200
to outlaw flamethrowers,

00:04:17.200 --> 00:04:18.660
though the bill remains stalled.

00:04:18.660 --> 00:04:21.340
And in 2015, 2018, and 2020,

00:04:21.340 --> 00:04:22.950
New York Congressman Elliot Engel

00:04:22.950 --> 00:04:24.400
sought to outlaw the possession

00:04:24.400 --> 00:04:25.620
or transfer of flamethrowers

00:04:25.620 --> 00:04:30.160
via the Flamethrowers? Really? Act.

00:04:30.160 --> 00:04:31.550
Yes, that is actually the name

00:04:31.550 --> 00:04:33.100
of the bill that he introduced.

00:04:33.100 --> 00:04:34.650
The bill never made it out of committee

00:04:34.650 --> 00:04:37.070
and Congressman Engle
left Congress in 2021

00:04:37.070 --> 00:04:38.500
after losing a primary challenge

00:04:38.500 --> 00:04:41.447
for reasons completely
unrelated to flamethrowers.

00:04:41.447 --> 00:04:42.340
But that takes us to your right

00:04:42.340 --> 00:04:44.180
to secretly record your conversations

00:04:44.180 --> 00:04:46.920
with third parties that
may or may not be related

00:04:46.920 --> 00:04:49.410
to conversations about flamethrowers.

00:04:49.410 --> 00:04:51.610
A common trope in film and TV involves

00:04:51.610 --> 00:04:53.620
characters secretly recording
their own conversations

00:04:53.620 --> 00:04:56.810
to catch a third party
admitting to criminal activity.

00:04:56.810 --> 00:04:58.723
- It's my word against yours.

00:04:59.830 --> 00:05:02.010
200 bucks a day, fluff.

00:05:02.010 --> 00:05:04.570
365 days a year since I was 12.

00:05:04.570 --> 00:05:06.280
- Actually it's your word against yours.

00:05:06.280 --> 00:05:07.540
- So therein lies the question.

00:05:07.540 --> 00:05:08.790
Can you actually do that?

00:05:08.790 --> 00:05:11.430
Well, to give everyone's favorite answer,

00:05:11.430 --> 00:05:13.170
it totally depends.

00:05:13.170 --> 00:05:15.050
Mostly depends on
whether you are violating

00:05:15.050 --> 00:05:17.480
any federal or state wiretapping laws.

00:05:17.480 --> 00:05:19.110
Federal law permits the recording

00:05:19.110 --> 00:05:21.150
of any phone call,
electronic communication,

00:05:21.150 --> 00:05:23.730
or in person conversation including video

00:05:23.730 --> 00:05:25.970
that captures audio with the consent

00:05:25.970 --> 00:05:28.490
of one of the parties to the conversation,

00:05:28.490 --> 00:05:30.760
also known as a one-party consent law.

00:05:30.760 --> 00:05:32.600
So under a one-party consent law

00:05:32.600 --> 00:05:34.530
you may record any conversation so long

00:05:34.530 --> 00:05:36.780
as you are a party to that conversation.

00:05:36.780 --> 00:05:39.280
You are that one party that can consent.

00:05:39.280 --> 00:05:41.090
If you are not a party
to the communication,

00:05:41.090 --> 00:05:42.450
then at least one person

00:05:42.450 --> 00:05:44.530
must give you consent to the recording

00:05:44.530 --> 00:05:46.670
or you may have committed the, you know,

00:05:46.670 --> 00:05:48.520
the crime of ease dropping.

00:05:48.520 --> 00:05:50.770
Now 38 states plus the
District of Columbia

00:05:50.770 --> 00:05:53.400
have adopted a one-party consent law.

00:05:53.400 --> 00:05:56.290
The remaining states though
have a two-party consent law.

00:05:56.290 --> 00:05:58.350
Now two-party consent
is a bit of a misnomer

00:05:58.350 --> 00:06:00.250
because you first have to get consent

00:06:00.250 --> 00:06:02.140
to every party to that conversation.

00:06:02.140 --> 00:06:03.720
So if there are three
parties to that conversation,

00:06:03.720 --> 00:06:05.540
you have to get consent from all three.

00:06:05.540 --> 00:06:07.040
And as a threshold matter,

00:06:07.040 --> 00:06:08.440
state and federal wiretapping laws

00:06:08.440 --> 00:06:10.260
only protect conversations
when the speaker

00:06:10.260 --> 00:06:12.420
has a reasonable expectation of privacy

00:06:12.420 --> 00:06:13.570
for the conversation.

00:06:13.570 --> 00:06:14.950
So for example, even though these things

00:06:14.950 --> 00:06:16.470
take place in public,

00:06:16.470 --> 00:06:18.110
people do have a reasonable expectation

00:06:18.110 --> 00:06:20.330
of privacy in a public bathroom stall

00:06:20.330 --> 00:06:22.730
or locker room in both
audio and video recordings

00:06:22.730 --> 00:06:24.670
in such a place would likely violate state

00:06:24.670 --> 00:06:27.270
and federal law without
the subject's consent.

00:06:27.270 --> 00:06:28.810
In contrast, though, a person bragging

00:06:28.810 --> 00:06:30.860
at a private party about cheating

00:06:30.860 --> 00:06:32.540
with a friend in a business deal,

00:06:32.540 --> 00:06:35.240
probably couldn't claim
a wiretap violation,

00:06:35.240 --> 00:06:38.290
even if this conversation was
recorded with a out consent.

00:06:38.290 --> 00:06:39.630
In addition, federal law,

00:06:39.630 --> 00:06:42.100
along with 17 one-party consent states

00:06:42.100 --> 00:06:43.590
prohibits the recording of conversations

00:06:43.590 --> 00:06:46.150
when done with criminal
or tortious intent.

00:06:46.150 --> 00:06:47.990
As an example, secretly
recording a conversation

00:06:47.990 --> 00:06:50.830
to use as blackmail would
probably not be protected.

00:06:50.830 --> 00:06:52.700
In contrast though, a
federal appeals court

00:06:52.700 --> 00:06:54.790
held that a son who used his phone

00:06:54.790 --> 00:06:56.570
to secretly record a conversation

00:06:56.570 --> 00:06:58.200
about his dying mother will

00:06:58.200 --> 00:07:00.160
could not be federally
prosecuted for wiretapping

00:07:00.160 --> 00:07:02.890
because the son lacked
tortious or criminal intent

00:07:02.890 --> 00:07:04.560
independent of the recording.

00:07:04.560 --> 00:07:06.550
Oh, and here's one more thing to consider.

00:07:06.550 --> 00:07:07.980
If your secretly recorded phone call

00:07:07.980 --> 00:07:09.810
takes place between two different states,

00:07:09.810 --> 00:07:11.160
you'd better ensure that both states

00:07:11.160 --> 00:07:12.850
are one-party consent jurisdictions

00:07:12.850 --> 00:07:14.980
or you could find
yourself in legal trouble.

00:07:14.980 --> 00:07:16.570
That's what happened to Linda Tripp.

00:07:16.570 --> 00:07:19.240
Back in the 1990s, government
employee, Linda Tripp,

00:07:19.240 --> 00:07:21.120
secretly recorded her
confidential phone calls

00:07:21.120 --> 00:07:23.460
with former White House
intern, Monica Lewinsky,

00:07:23.460 --> 00:07:25.860
wherein Ms. Lewinsky
provided salacious details

00:07:25.860 --> 00:07:27.210
about her intimate relationship

00:07:27.210 --> 00:07:28.350
with then President Bill Clinton.

00:07:28.350 --> 00:07:29.970
Now these tapes became a public sensation

00:07:29.970 --> 00:07:31.920
upon their release and the
fallout from the scandal

00:07:31.920 --> 00:07:33.950
resulted in President
Clinton's impeachment,

00:07:33.950 --> 00:07:36.170
where, of course, he was
acquitted by the Senate.

00:07:36.170 --> 00:07:38.280
Now here's where Linda Tripp found herself

00:07:38.280 --> 00:07:39.710
the target for prosecution.

00:07:39.710 --> 00:07:42.790
Though, D.C. is a one-party
recording jurisdiction,

00:07:42.790 --> 00:07:44.710
Linda Tripp recorded
her calls for Maryland,

00:07:44.710 --> 00:07:46.990
which requires all parties to consent.

00:07:46.990 --> 00:07:49.050
In January, 1998, Ms. Tripp turned over

00:07:49.050 --> 00:07:50.880
the tapes to independent
counsel Kenneth Starr

00:07:50.880 --> 00:07:52.090
and exchange for immunity.

00:07:52.090 --> 00:07:54.830
However, Maryland prosecutors
indicted Ms. Tripp

00:07:54.830 --> 00:07:57.050
on state wiretapping charges anyway,

00:07:57.050 --> 00:07:58.290
arguing that federal immunity

00:07:58.290 --> 00:08:00.320
did not extend to state violations.

00:08:00.320 --> 00:08:01.810
But before that trial,
the judge ruled that

00:08:01.810 --> 00:08:04.040
Ms. Lewinsky whose
testimony the state needed

00:08:04.040 --> 00:08:05.840
to prove Tripp broke the law

00:08:05.840 --> 00:08:07.600
would be barred from testifying.

00:08:07.600 --> 00:08:08.970
And without their star witness,

00:08:08.970 --> 00:08:11.530
the state dropped all
charges in May of 2000.

00:08:11.530 --> 00:08:13.740
So your mileage may vary.

00:08:13.740 --> 00:08:15.160
And that takes us to one of my favorite

00:08:15.160 --> 00:08:16.670
American rights of all time.

00:08:16.670 --> 00:08:18.980
That is the right to
steal someone's house.

00:08:18.980 --> 00:08:21.590
Yes, that actually a thing.

00:08:21.590 --> 00:08:22.790
One of the most important rights

00:08:22.790 --> 00:08:24.060
that come with being a homeowner

00:08:24.060 --> 00:08:25.780
is the right to keep unwanted intruders

00:08:25.780 --> 00:08:26.950
off your property.

00:08:26.950 --> 00:08:28.560
In fact, a person that knowingly enters

00:08:28.560 --> 00:08:30.430
your property without
permission has committed

00:08:30.430 --> 00:08:33.010
a trespass and is subject
to immediate arrest.

00:08:33.010 --> 00:08:35.070
But here's an interesting wrinkle.

00:08:35.070 --> 00:08:37.770
If you commit trespass
for a day, you go to jail,

00:08:37.770 --> 00:08:40.260
but if you openly trespass for years,

00:08:40.260 --> 00:08:43.230
well, congratulations,
you now own that land

00:08:43.230 --> 00:08:45.050
and any buildings that are on top of it.

00:08:45.050 --> 00:08:45.883
That's right.

00:08:45.883 --> 00:08:47.100
You can actually crime your way

00:08:47.100 --> 00:08:48.670
into becoming a property owner

00:08:48.670 --> 00:08:50.130
in certain circumstances.

00:08:50.130 --> 00:08:52.480
But fair warning, this is not an advisable

00:08:52.480 --> 00:08:54.530
or easy way to earn title to property

00:08:54.530 --> 00:08:56.600
as it usually takes decades of trespass

00:08:56.600 --> 00:08:59.500
and fulfilling other state
specific requirements

00:08:59.500 --> 00:09:01.820
for that property to
actually change ownership.

00:09:01.820 --> 00:09:04.770
All right, so for purely
informational purposes,

00:09:04.770 --> 00:09:06.650
here is how a would-be-house-thief

00:09:06.650 --> 00:09:08.200
could actually do this.

00:09:08.200 --> 00:09:10.620
Under a doctrine that's
called adverse possession,

00:09:10.620 --> 00:09:12.680
a trespasser who continuously possesses

00:09:12.680 --> 00:09:15.420
or occupies real property
for certain length of time

00:09:15.420 --> 00:09:16.930
can actually acquire legal ownership

00:09:16.930 --> 00:09:19.610
to the property that
they're illegally occupying.

00:09:19.610 --> 00:09:21.180
To invoke adverse possessions

00:09:21.180 --> 00:09:22.120
sufficient to get ownership,

00:09:22.120 --> 00:09:23.490
the trespassers occupation on the land

00:09:23.490 --> 00:09:25.140
must meet certain requirements.

00:09:25.140 --> 00:09:26.250
It must be hostile.

00:09:26.250 --> 00:09:28.160
It must be done without
permission of the owner.

00:09:28.160 --> 00:09:28.993
It must be actual.

00:09:28.993 --> 00:09:30.500
So they have to be physically present.

00:09:30.500 --> 00:09:32.240
It has to be open and notorious,

00:09:32.240 --> 00:09:34.330
the act trespassing can't be secret

00:09:34.330 --> 00:09:35.980
and must be obvious to onlookers.

00:09:35.980 --> 00:09:37.570
And the trespasser must be in possession

00:09:37.570 --> 00:09:39.910
of the property for an
uninterrupted period of time

00:09:39.910 --> 00:09:42.670
as prescribed by whatever
statute we're in.

00:09:42.670 --> 00:09:44.730
The time period for
vesting varies by state,

00:09:44.730 --> 00:09:47.290
ranging from five to 30 years,

00:09:47.290 --> 00:09:49.020
but most commonly 10 to 20 years

00:09:49.020 --> 00:09:51.740
is required of actual trespassing.

00:09:51.740 --> 00:09:53.770
Some states require
payment of property taxes

00:09:53.770 --> 00:09:55.010
during the occupation period,

00:09:55.010 --> 00:09:57.750
others mandate physical
improvements to the land.

00:09:57.750 --> 00:09:59.490
And some states even
require the trespasser

00:09:59.490 --> 00:10:01.650
to produce some kind of document or deed

00:10:01.650 --> 00:10:03.430
relating to the ownership of the property,

00:10:03.430 --> 00:10:05.140
even if the document itself is inaccurate

00:10:05.140 --> 00:10:06.710
or carries no legal weight.

00:10:06.710 --> 00:10:07.760
Now you might be asking,

00:10:07.760 --> 00:10:09.960
why in the world would every state

00:10:09.960 --> 00:10:12.640
give people the right
to legally steal land,

00:10:12.640 --> 00:10:14.850
albeit very, very slowly?

00:10:14.850 --> 00:10:16.360
Well, the concept of adverse possession

00:10:16.360 --> 00:10:19.040
actually dates back to
6th century Roman law.

00:10:19.040 --> 00:10:20.750
Adverse possession was
designed to encourage

00:10:20.750 --> 00:10:22.190
land owners to make beneficial

00:10:22.190 --> 00:10:23.620
and efficient use of their land,

00:10:23.620 --> 00:10:25.340
thereby allowing title to pass

00:10:25.340 --> 00:10:27.210
to the individual taking care of the land

00:10:27.210 --> 00:10:29.640
from the holder that is
effectively abandoned it.

00:10:29.640 --> 00:10:30.840
Today the primary justification

00:10:30.840 --> 00:10:32.530
for adverse possession is to incentivize

00:10:32.530 --> 00:10:34.330
land owners to settle title disputes

00:10:34.330 --> 00:10:36.360
by putting statutes of limitations

00:10:36.360 --> 00:10:38.500
on possible litigation and possession.

00:10:38.500 --> 00:10:41.170
In other words, if we don't
really know who owns the land,

00:10:41.170 --> 00:10:43.960
it's a good idea to give
clean title to someone

00:10:43.960 --> 00:10:45.950
who has had the land for a very long time

00:10:45.950 --> 00:10:47.880
and often made improvements to it.

00:10:47.880 --> 00:10:49.900
It removes a cloud of title.

00:10:49.900 --> 00:10:51.760
So to summarize, I am not telling you

00:10:51.760 --> 00:10:53.760
all to commit years of criminal trespass

00:10:53.760 --> 00:10:55.860
to maybe acquire real property,

00:10:55.860 --> 00:10:58.990
but if you've already been
committing criminal trespass

00:10:58.990 --> 00:11:00.530
